    """G3/G4: run an ordered batch of independent rollback items, all or nothing.

    Nothing is shared between different items -- each carries its own graph,
    applied journal and retain set. G4 adds idempotency: an item whose
    `operation_id` repeats an earlier item with identical request data is a
    retry, answered with the first item's result, counted once. The batch is
    processed in phases so that every failure is reported at its own index in
    the required order:

    1. envelope and per-item structure, including `operation_id`
       (invalid-batch / invalid-batch-item);
    2. duplicate and conflict detection (conflicting-operation);
    3. a new ID runs its own G2 checks and calculation
